\section*{Uniform bi-Hölder transport under weak MTW}

\subsection{OpenAI's claim}
\textit{Uniform bi-Hölder transport under weak MTW}: For a fixed compact weak-MTW manifold, the manuscript claims one Hölder modulus for optimal maps and their inverses over all density pairs with common positive lower and finite upper bounds. No density smoothness or absence of conjugate cut points is assumed.

\subsection{Outline of the argument}
\textit{Uniform bi-Hölder transport under weak MTW}: Lifted gap sections of transport potentials are studied in the tangent injectivity domain. Convexity turns a uniform power estimate on dual-potential oscillation into a diameter estimate on their endpoint images. Taking the supremum over all admissible densities gives one class-wide bound, and comparison at nearby poles supplies Hölder continuity in both transport directions.

\subsection{Scope relative to this problem}
\textit{Uniform bi-Hölder transport under weak MTW}: For a fixed compact weak-MTW manifold, the manuscript claims one Hölder modulus for optimal maps and their inverses over all density pairs with common positive lower and finite upper bounds. No density smoothness or absence of conjugate cut points is assumed. The parameters, regularity assumptions and normalization in this question are retained in applying that assertion.

With the hypotheses and conventions above, the claimed result addresses the whole mathematical assertion on this page.

\subsection{Formal verification}
Family 360 describes Lean coverage for injectivity-domain convexity, global support and the listed finite-family estimates, as well as uniform bi-Hölder transport; arbitrary-potential local injectivity is broader.

\textit{Uniform bi-Hölder transport under weak MTW}: The manuscript links \texttt{BiholderTransport.lean} (declaration \texttt{OAI.WeakMTWTransport.uniform\_biHolder\_transport}), \texttt{WeakMTWGlobalSupport.lean} (declaration \texttt{OAI.WeakMTWGlobalSupport.current\_main\_convexity}).

The documented selection includes this manuscript’s main assertion; that assertion retains the restrictions stated above.

This site has not run the Lean development. These links describe OpenAI’s selected formal statements and should be read with their stated scope.

\subsection{Status caveat}
OpenAI reports that an internal model produced the manuscripts. Their arguments have not been independently verified as proofs by this site. Any portion outside the documented formal scope may contain mistakes, and the catalogue label reports the announced mathematical claim.

